.TH CLIPMUNGE 1 "2026-09-09" "clipmunge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipmunge \- rewrite the Wayland clipboard using Lua rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipmunge
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clipmunge
watches the clipboard and applies rules from a Lua config file.
Rules can remove tracking parameters from URLs or provide a link as HTML
while preserving a ticket number as plain text.
.PP
Requires a compositor supporting
.BR ext-data-control-v1 .
Only text and rich text are currently processed; PRIMARY is ignored.
A config file is required. There are no built-in rules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Load \fIPATH\fR instead of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clipmunge/config.lua .
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the config and regular expressions, then exit without connecting
to a compositor.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-reload
Disable automatic config reloading.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Disable the notification command.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Log incoming selections and rewrites, including clipboard content.
UTF-8 payload previews include at most 512 input bytes each. Non-UTF-8 payloads
show their size only. Own and secret-marked offers are skipped before reading.
.IP
.B Logs may contain passwords or other private text.
Without this flag, payload diagnostics show MIME types and byte counts.
Lua print output and error messages are not redacted and may contain copied text.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and the default config path, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH RELOADING
Changes in the config directory reload the rules after about 150 milliseconds
of inactivity. Changes to neighbouring Lua modules also trigger a reload.
A failed reload is logged and the previous rules remain active.
.PP
At startup, the given and resolved config directories are watched unless
read-only or inaccessible. If neither can be watched, automatic reload is
disabled with a warning.
The config symlink is resolved on every load, but watches are not updated.
Restart after removing a watched directory or moving the target into a new
editable directory to watch that location.
.SH SECURITY
Only install configs you trust. A config can set
.B notify_command
to run a program with rule output as an argument.
No shell is used by clipmunge to interpret those arguments.
.B \-\-no\-notify
disables this mechanism.
.PP
The Lua interpreter excludes
.BR io ,
.BR os ,
.B debug
and
.BR coroutine .
The globals
.BR load ,
.BR loadfile ,
.B dofile
and
.B collectgarbage
are removed; C module loading is disabled.
.B require
uses a search path initially set to the config directories. Lua can change
.BR package.path .
These restrictions do not confine all file access or make arbitrary configs safe.
.PP
Lua execution has an instruction budget of roughly ten million instructions
per config execution or handler call and a 64 MiB Lua heap limit.
The instruction hook does not bound time spent in native functions.
A failed handler is logged and skipped.
Notifications are limited to 200 characters and one per published rewrite.
.PP
Selections advertising
.B x-kde-passwordManagerHint
are skipped before reading, including under
.BR \-\-debug .
The list is configurable through
.B secret_mimes
in
.BR clipmunge (5).
Applications may omit the hint. clipmunge does not otherwise recognise
passwords, and any secret matching a rule may be rewritten.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The Wayland display to connect to.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Config base directory. If unset, empty or relative, use
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
Systemd notification socket. If set, clipmunge sends
.B READY=1
after loading the config and connecting to the compositor.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Override the log level, for example
.IR RUST_LOG=debug .
This alone does not enable clipboard content diagnostics; those require
.BR \-\-debug .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-zero for startup failures or loss of the data device.
A failed rule or reload is logged without stopping the daemon.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clipmunge/config.lua
Rules and settings. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/clipmunge/config.lua .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clipmunge (5),
.BR notify-send (1)
